{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Client",
    "description": "Buyers, their orders, and the styles under them.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Add Order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/{{client_id}}/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients",
            "{{client_id}}",
            "orders"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Add another order (new unique order_number) to an existing client.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"order_number\": \"\",\n  \"order_date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"delivery_deadline\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"sea_cutoff_date\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"ship_mode\": \"sea\",\n  \"currency\": \"\",\n  \"agent\": \"\",\n  \"line\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Client Orders",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/{{client_id}}/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients",
            "{{client_id}}",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "Rows to return (1-200).",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "One client's orders. PAGED \u2014 each row eager-loads its styles and their\nSKUs, so an unpaged call on a long-standing customer pulled their whole\ncatalogue three levels deep."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Create Client",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients"
          ]
        },
        "description": "",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"country\": \"\",\n  \"order_number\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Deletable",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/{{client_id}}/deletable",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients",
            "{{client_id}}",
            "deletable"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "CAN this client be deleted, and if not, what exactly is in the way?\n\nThe same check DELETE runs, without doing anything \u2014 so a screen can grey\nthe button out and say why, instead of offering it and then explaining a\n409. `blockers` is [{table, count, what}]; empty means the delete will go\nthrough."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Delete Client",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/{{client_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients",
            "{{client_id}}"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Delete a client that has produced NOTHING \u2014 a mistyped or duplicate row.\n\nNEITHER AN ORDER NOR A STYLE IS A REASON TO REFUSE. Creating a client also\ncreates its first order (order_number is required on POST /clients), and a\nbreakdown upload adds styles and SKUs that may never have been made from;\nall of those cascade away with the customer. What refuses the delete is a\nrow recording real WORK \u2014 a minted garment, a logged production event, a\nwage rate or a paid wage line \u2014 and the 409 now names which and how many,\nrather than guessing at \"a style rate, a supplier PO, a cutting entry\".\n\nAsk GET /clients/{id}/deletable first if you want to know before pressing it.\n\nDM only, matching client creation. MD passes as superuser."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Client",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/{{client_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients",
            "{{client_id}}"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "One client \u2014 what an edit form loads before it saves.\n\nA CLIENT login may read only itself, matching /{client_id}/orders."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Clients",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "clients"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "include_inactive",
              "value": "False",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "Rows to return (1-200).",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "H1: a CLIENT login sees only its own row. The sibling endpoints in this\nfile already pin the caller; this one did not, so a customer could read the\nwhole customer list.\n\nDeactivated clients are hidden by default \u2014 that is what deactivation is\nfor. Pass `include_inactive=true` to get them back (an admin screen listing\neveryone, or a lookup by a client who has since been switched off).\n\nPAGED. The CLIENT-role narrowing is now part of the QUERY rather than a\nfilter applied to the result: paging a list and then filtering it would\nreturn one row alongside a `total` that counted every other customer."
      },
      "response": []
    },
